@talks pool
topic: ship
// TW1, the Talk a while pack: shared pool, topic ship (the Wren herself). Facts from content/facts.md, sections 1-2.

== hum
them: Listen. You hear that hum? That's the Wren, thinking.
them: You stop hearing it after a week. Then you miss it on leave.
ask: What do you think of her so far? The Wren?
listen: Does she ever go quiet?
  them: Almost never. If she does, Works is already running.   #funny
share: I like her. She feels lived in.
  them: Lived in. That's it exactly. She's a home.   #warm
cheer: She's lovely. Bit far from the shops.
  them: The crew store's a shop! Sort of. It has socks.   #funny

== favourite-spot
them: Found a favourite spot aboard yet? Everyone has one.
them: Mine changes. Right now it's a seat by a window.
ask: Where do you go when you want a bit of quiet?
listen: Which window?
  them: I'm not telling. Then it wouldn't be quiet.   #funny
share: My bunk, with a book.
  them: A bunk and a book. The smallest holiday aboard. Perfect.
cheer: The mess. Right by the toast.
  them: That's not quiet. That's breakfast. Still counts.   #funny

== smells
when: !who:sato|brennan|calder
them: Every deck smells different. Have you noticed?
them: Five is oil. Three is toast. The garden's rain.
ask: Which deck's your favourite smell?
listen: What does Deck 2 smell of?
  them: Paper and polish. And whatever Sato's brewing.   #funny
share: Three. Toast, every time.
  them: Correct answer. Brennan would be proud.
cheer: Five. I like oil. Is that odd?
  them: Very Works of you. Calder would approve. Quietly.   #funny

== corners
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: I still find corners I've never seen. After all this time.
them: Last week, a little seat behind a pipe. Someone had left a cushion.
ask: What's the oddest place you've found aboard?
listen: Whose cushion was it?
  them: No idea. I left it there. It's someone's secret.   #warm
share: I'm still finding the normal places.
  them: That's fine. The odd ones find you later.
cheer: The way back to my bunk. Daily.
  them: The ship moves the corridors at night. Everyone knows.   #funny

== lift
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:kovac-zainab|cruz-tove|keane-davi
them: The lift's the heart of the ship, really. Everyone meets in it.
them: "Four, please." I say it in my sleep.   #funny
ask: Who's the best person you've shared the lift with?
listen: Who do you meet in it most?
  them: The same five people. We nod. It's a club now.   #funny
share: Someone who told me where everything was.
  them: Lift guides. The best kind. Pass it on.
cheer: Myself. Reflected in the door.
  them: Good company. Doesn't talk back.   #funny

== creaks
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: She creaks at night, the Wren. Little ticks and settles.
them: Old ships talk. She's just telling us she's fine.
ask: Do the night noises bother you?
listen: How old is she?
  them: Old enough to have stories. Young enough to keep going.
share: Not any more. I like them now.
  them: Me too. It's like rain on a roof. Nearly.   #warm
cheer: Only when they sound like footsteps.
  them: That's the Watch on rounds. Probably.   #funny

== portraits
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:marrow
them: Have you looked at the portrait gallery on Deck 2?
them: Every captain the Wren's had. All very serious.
ask: Do you ever wonder about the people who were here before us?
listen: Which captain do you like best?
  them: Varga. Started the gallery. Looks like they're about to laugh.
share: Yes. Who sat in my bunk before me.
  them: Somebody who left it fine for you. That's the deal, really.   #warm
cheer: Only whether they had better biscuits.
  them: Unknowable. But probably not. Brennan's are the best.   #funny

== windows
when: tier>=colleague
them: There's a window aboard where the stars just pour past.
them: I stood there twenty minutes once. Forgot I was going somewhere.
ask: What do you think about, looking out there?
listen: Where were you going?
  them: Dinner. I was late. Totally worth it.   #funny
share: Home, mostly. How far it is.
  them: Far. But the stars are the same ones. Some of them.   #warm
cheer: Whether anyone's looking back at us.
  them: Waving, probably. Wave back. Just in case.   #funny

== kind-ship
when: tier>=colleague !who:brennan
them: She's old, but she's kind, the Wren. Like a good boot.   #funny
them: She's had seventy-odd people at a time in her for years. You feel it.
ask: What makes a ship good, do you think? Not the engines.
listen: Has she always been like this?
  them: Longer than anyone aboard can say. Ask the portraits.
share: The people. Always the people.
  them: Right answer. The engines are just how we get about.   #warm
cheer: A good mess. Everything else follows.
  them: Brennan would agree. Loudly.   #funny

== leave-her
when: tier>=friend !who:tomas|marrow|brennan !thread:leaving
them: Sometimes I wonder how I'll feel the day I leave her. Silly.
them: Not soon. Not planning to. Just, one day. Everyone does.
ask: Do you think you'll stay on the Wren a long time?
listen: What would you miss most?
  them: The people. Then the hum. Then the toast, honestly.   #warm
share: I hope so. I'd like to.
  them: Good. I'd like that too. Selfishly.   #warm
cheer: They'll have to carry me off.
  them: I'll help carry. Slowly. Very slowly.   #funny
